WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.393
- Kids'...
(Kelly chortles)

00:00:01.393 --> 00:00:02.226
(beep)

00:00:02.226 --> 00:00:03.730
Kids' pictures with Santa.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.830
I actually have a great story.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.351
I need to find this one
Santa and apologize.

00:00:08.351 --> 00:00:09.184
(Kelly chuckles)

00:00:09.184 --> 00:00:10.017
(buzzer)

00:00:10.017 --> 00:00:12.684
(festive music)

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:15.780
All right, everybody,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.613
if you know me at all,

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:17.910
you know I love Christmas.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:18.760
I really, really do.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:19.810
It's my favorite holiday.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:20.643
It's so much fun.

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:21.476
I love the music.

00:00:21.476 --> 00:00:22.630
I love the music so much, in fact,

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.900
I'm actually releasing
a second Christmas album

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.280
that comes out today.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.010
And why are we releasing it
in October before Halloween?

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.850
Because why the hell not?

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.270
And because you only get so long

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.010
to listen to Christmas music.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.210
I'm very excited about the album,

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:37.610
it's called "When
Christmas Comes Around..."

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:40.790
because everybody's in a different place,

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:43.150
and it depends on the year
and chapter of your life.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:45.410
And there's literally a song for every

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.290
kind of emotion you might be having.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:48.240
There's sad, there's happy,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.560
there's let's go out and
get a Christmas tree,

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.630
and then there's sexy.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:52.930
There's all these different songs.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:54.140
There's some originals,

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.040
and then there's also some classics.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.090
My new single for it,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.510
which is "Christmas Isn't
Canceled (Just You)",

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:01.870
I actually don't believe
in cancel culture.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:05.130
It was just a funny play off of like

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.580
maybe your relationship went sour

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.150
or maybe everything isn't going okay.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:11.730
That doesn't mean everything is bad.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.530
Christmas is coming and it's not canceled,

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.790
just maybe a portion of your life.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.930
To celebrate the release of my new album,

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.341
its first single, "Christmas
Isn't Canceled (Just You)",

00:01:19.341 --> 00:01:20.300
in the holidays,

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.300
I'm going to play a
fun holiday game called

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:25.860
Christmas Isn't Canceled...
But What Should Be?

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.183
Pumpkin spice lattes?

00:01:28.183 --> 00:01:29.690
(ding)
With almond milk, please.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.120
Because I'm lactose intolerant.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.250
I love pumpkin, I love
spice, and I love a latte.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.650
So definitely liking that, yep.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.680
I love all Christmas drinks.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:41.160
I love having a Christmas drink in June

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.123
and feeling like it's Christmas.

00:01:42.123 --> 00:01:44.340
It's just as nice.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.880
Okay, elf on a shelf.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.360
Love elf on a shelf.
(ding)

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.920
We'll say that,

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.810
man, that elf works hard

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.490
on all those little scenarios.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.060
That elf is just going fishing sometimes.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.930
He shows up, and he's been at soccer camp.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.620
He's... There's a lot of things.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.130
He's scaling a wall.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:02.250
Like that elf...

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.180
It's a lot of hard work parents, right?

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:06.380
We're thinking those
elves work really hard.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.320
But I will say it's really fun,

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.000
and I love when the elf visits,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.040
and it's magical so.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.440
All right, so decorating for Christmas

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.190
much earlier than December.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.049
Than December?

00:02:18.049 --> 00:02:18.882
(ding)

00:02:18.882 --> 00:02:20.460
Of course you're
decorating before December.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.940
Do you know how much money
you spend on those lights

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:23.110
and those decorations?

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.910
I think it's fine to start...

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.450
I decorate my house big time.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:29.110
Usually we start November 1st.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.350
Because it's, you get two full months

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.360
of all the prettiness.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.580
Because I love Christmas,

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.280
and it makes you feel happy, right?

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.330
You're coming in your driveway,

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:38.180
it's all lit up.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.140
It's magical.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.557
I'm liking that.

00:02:40.557 --> 00:02:44.180
"Die Hard" being considered
a Christmas movie?

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.260
Absolutely!
(ding)

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.740
They're at a Christmas party.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.720
He rescues them at a Christmas party.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.400
Anything with Alan Rickman,

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.670
even Harry Potter, okay?

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:54.503
He's in that too.

00:02:54.503 --> 00:02:58.190
But I will say "Die Hard" is
definitely one of my faves.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:02:59.940
All of them, all the "Die Hards".

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.600
Of course it's a Christmas classic.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.290
Get outta here.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:04.440
Eggnog?

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.830
Yes.
(ding)

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.710
Nothing is being canceled today people.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:08.543
You know why?

00:03:08.543 --> 00:03:10.010
I shouldn't drink eggnog

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:12.410
because it can upset my tummy,

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.760
but they have almond eggnog now.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.620
They have different kinds of eggnog now.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.700
But you know what's really not canceled?

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.970
Spiked eggnog.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.360
I will say,

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.820
what is canceled
(buzzer)

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:25.553
is what might happen to
me after drinking eggnog.

00:03:25.553 --> 00:03:28.010
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:29.780
Ugly Christmas sweaters?

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.060
What?
(ding)

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.190
Ugly Christmas sweaters are always funny.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.530
And it's also a time like

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.410
I feel like everybody,

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:37.243
maybe it's just me,

00:03:37.243 --> 00:03:40.450
but I have to get dressed up
all the time for work, okay?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.520
So you know what? No.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.710
If my family's coming over,

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:45.070
you have to love me regardless, okay?

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:48.530
So yeah, you're gonna
love me in my sweats.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.420
Why am I dressing up for you?

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.240
Like why would I do that?

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.626
Black Friday shopping crowds?

00:03:54.626 --> 00:03:56.120
(buzzer)
Looking at you, mom.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:56.988
This is why it's canceled, okay?

00:03:56.988 --> 00:03:57.970
(buzzer)

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:00.330
It was a Walmart and it
was in Burleson, Texas.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.817
And my mom was like,

00:04:01.817 --> 00:04:02.860
"We gotta get there early

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:04.120
because the deals..."
(Kelly gargles)

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:05.250
And she dragged me there.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:08.210
I had to fight grown men and women.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:13.210
I was a freshman in high school
fighting off for this TV.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.120
People get crazy.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.250
I'm like, it's not that great of a deal.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:22.240
My God, to sacrifice your
character and one's dignity.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.970
Like geez!

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:26.090
But I will say, it's awesome now

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.810
because they do a lot of it online.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:28.860
That's cool

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:30.243
because then you don't
have to leave your couch,

00:04:30.243 --> 00:04:32.520
and you can be in your
ugly Christmas sweater

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.570
drinking some eggnog.
(Kelly chuckles)

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.100
Last-minute Christmas present wrapping?

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.160
Not a fan.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:38.993
Not a fan.
(buzzer)

00:04:38.993 --> 00:04:41.650
I know that sometimes it happens

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:42.550
maybe with one or two gifts,

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:43.470
that's acceptable.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:44.580
But canceled in general.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.810
Like I...

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:47.100
The end of the year for me

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.010
is my busiest time with all the jobs.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:54.240
And I generally am done very early.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:55.757
Early.

00:04:55.757 --> 00:04:57.440
I mean, I'm usually a month in advance.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.010
I love wrapping Christmas presents.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:00.160
It's an art form.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.000
It's not just wrapping paper.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.080
It's selected wrapping
paper for each gift,

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.570
and also there's jute rope involved,

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.300
and also those little things added to it.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.220
It's a lot, and I love it.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.210
My favorite wrapping though,

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.130
and I've changed it up

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:14.070
because I know I have children
that like bright and fun,

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.010
like whatever.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:19.120
But my favorite is just a
good old parchment paper,

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:20.340
wrapped with jute rope,

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:23.551
and a little reindeer
thingy hanging off of it,

00:05:23.551 --> 00:05:25.002
maybe some jingle bells.
(bells jingles)

00:05:25.002 --> 00:05:27.650
I like a really classic look,

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:28.720
but I do have children,

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:32.330
so I spice it up with some fun stuff too.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.960
Kids'...
(Kelly chortles)

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.880
Kids' pictures with Santa.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.800
I actually have a great story for that.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.263
I need to find this one
Santa and apologize.

00:05:42.263 --> 00:05:43.670
(Kelly chuckles)
(buzzer)

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:44.760
I think this should be canceled

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:46.710
because it's a, ugh,

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:47.800
it's a big thing.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.400
And then a lot of times you end up crying,

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.430
or it's just like,

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.780
they change their gifts
when they talk to him.

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:53.613
And you're like, Santa,

00:05:53.613 --> 00:05:55.390
maybe he doesn't have time to run around

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:56.223
and get different ones.

00:05:56.223 --> 00:05:58.470
I don't know, like Santa's busy.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.030
It was either last year
or the year before,

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:03.080
I took my kids with my
friend Trisha to go see,

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.240
and my friend Trisha had to go

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.700
because I couldn't drive
because I hurt myself.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.960
It's like we end up in here,

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:10.340
it's chaos getting through.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.120
We're supposed to follow
this story on our thing.

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.230
We missed it somehow...

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:14.063
I don't know what hap...

00:06:14.063 --> 00:06:15.920
It was just really hard to follow the app

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.240
or it wasn't connecting.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:20.090
Everything and my kids were
like wining at some point.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:21.150
It just was chaos.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:22.740
And then by the time we
get there, all of a sudden,

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:25.200
she's like, "Oh, we get out of the car".

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.430
And so then, I'm hurt,
with a crutch, right?

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.640
Hurt, and I'm like...

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:33.390
There are all these cars behind
us the whole time, right?

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.040
The whole time there's
all these cars behind us.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:35.873
So I'm like, "Oh my god".

00:06:35.873 --> 00:06:36.706
I'm panicking, I'm sweating.

00:06:36.706 --> 00:06:38.910
I'm gonna be like hopping to Santa.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.440
I walk just on my foot, just whatever,

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:42.650
adrenaline kicks in.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:44.660
Trisha's like, "Why are you walking?"

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:46.320
The kids, I'm rushing over.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:47.500
Santa is just like,

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.670
first of all, you can't be
with him because of COVID,

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:51.820
so it's like the weirdest
Santa picture ever.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:53.040
He's like over there,

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:53.873
and we're like here,

00:06:53.873 --> 00:06:55.070
and we're pretending he's there.

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:56.170
And the kids don't get it.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:57.340
They're so young.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:59.150
And then I'm just like, "Stand there!"

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:00.225
It was chaos.

00:07:00.225 --> 00:07:01.058
(guy behind camera laughs)

00:07:01.058 --> 00:07:02.120
I yelled at Santa.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:03.460
I did yell at Santa.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:04.740
Not hardcore,

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.320
but I was definitely...

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.420
I reprimanded Santa.
(Kelly chuckles)

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.000
Because he was asking a lot,

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:10.950
and my kids were so young,

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.500
and I was like, "What
is your damage, Santa?"

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.780
Like what...

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.990
They're like four and six, dude.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.770
And they don't understand
why you're over there.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:19.603
It was hard.

00:07:19.603 --> 00:07:21.470
And then my foot, and it was a lot.

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:25.085
But to that Santa who
totally thinks I'm crazy,

00:07:25.085 --> 00:07:26.770
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:28.220
I'm sorry.

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:30.160
It wasn't very magical,

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.550
but we're probably gonna
do it again this year.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:35.020
(Kelly laughs loudly)

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:35.853
All right, y'all,

00:07:35.853 --> 00:07:37.310
thank you so much for hanging out with me.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:38.430
You know what's not canceled?

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.400
My awesome new album.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.770
It's called "When Christmas Comes Around".

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:44.250
I hope you dig it.

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:45.120
We worked really hard on it.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.990
It's a very different
kind of Christmas album

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:48.700
than you're probably used to,

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:51.030
but it's where I was at in my life.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.330
So I enjoyed making it,

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:54.320
and if you don't like it,

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.774
you're getting coal in your stocking.

00:07:55.774 --> 00:07:57.260
(Kelly laughs)
(festive music)

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:58.093
Goodbye.

